          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I am 34 weeks pregnant with swelling in my hands and a headache that will not shift. How urgent is this, and what should I be asking about?",
          "answer": "Please seek medical assessment today.\n\nA new headache during pregnancy, especially when combined with swelling, is a pattern that warrants same-day medical assessment (red-flag-sudden-severe-headache). This is not a diagnosis, but rather an indication that these symptoms together require timely medical review.\n\nYour symptoms involve a headache, which relates to your neurological system, and swelling in your hands, which relates to fluid balance in your body. When these two symptoms occur together during pregnancy, a clinician would want to rule out conditions such as pre-eclampsia.\n\nYou should discuss with your clinician the urgency of these symptoms, and ask what conditions they are checking for given your pregnancy status, headache, and swelling.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
